"""Storyboard source for P4, the pin tumbler lock (v1, 2026-11-25, overnight run).
build_scenes.py turns this into scenes.json, timing every scene from the narration's word timestamps.
Anchors are the first words of the scene's narration, lowercase, as spoken in script/narration.txt.

Tools: "motion-canvas" (2D), "blender" (3D hero: scenes/blender/l1_lock.py, `mode` field), "archival" (a public-domain still
from research/assets.json, prepared by tools/research/prep_assets_p4.py into scenes/assets/, shown in a chalk frame with a
credit line, slow push-in).

Colour meanings for this episode (style bible: meanings never change):
  chalk   structure: shell, plug, key, doors, buildings, engravings' frames
  violet  the working part: the pins and the shear line; a gap that lands on the line glows violet
  muted   blocked, failed, wrong, "not a pin lock"
  orange (heat) and lime (electricity) are NOT used. No arrowheads; direction by motion, dashes and travelling dots.
Locator (top-right, small): a chalk lock silhouette with the current act: "1 · what it checks", "2 · 1851", "3 · the bargain".
Michael's standing notes: hook first (S00a-S00e: our own animation, no photo or archival before the sting), 1 s beat after the
first line, soft landing into the sting after S00e, every named person gets a who-were-they line (Blaze, Potts, Pitt-Rivers,
Yale Sr., Yale Jr., Bramah, Hobbs; Chubb is named as a firm/lock maker with his patent).
Safety: conceptual only. No pick tools, no tension tools, no hands, no step sequences on screen.
"""

